# TASK-260715-3kjhkw review verdict

Verdict: changes requested for Change Request `CR-TASK-260715-3kjhkw-1`, revision 1, candidate tree `8958e24c14157b65906d87bd3e9136b217b4bc5c`.

## Required change

`MemoryWatermarkController.nextState` permits a fresh memory-warning observation to recover an existing `.pressure` state to `.soft`. At `MemoryWatermarkController.swift:509-526`, entry severity only short-circuits when it is greater than the current state. A warning produces `.pressure` at line 535, but warning is not part of `allSignalsPermitRecovery` at lines 567-583. Therefore, with healthy byte signals and satisfied dwell, a warning at current `.pressure` falls through to recovery. This contradicts the required deterministic maximum-signal transition and means an actual warning can reduce pressure severity.

The production call site under review is `MemoryWatermarkController.observe` calling `nextState` at lines 374-379. Existing test coverage only checks warning entry from `.normal` and a rate-limited warning burst; it does not exercise warning concurrent with an eligible recovery.

An isolated negative test, `warningCannotRecoverBelowPressure`, first enters `.pressure`, advances beyond the event interval, then submits a fresh `.memoryWarning` with healthy samples. It expects the state to remain `.pressure` and no recovery transition. The candidate instead returns `.soft` with `MemoryWatermarkTransition(from: .pressure, to: .soft, reason: .recovery)`. Exit code: 1, two expectation failures. Evidence log: `.temp/TASK-260715-3kjhkw/memory-warning-negative-test.log`.

