## State trace

- Inclusive maximum-signal entry: Normal -> Soft -> Pressure -> Critical.
- Strict-above exits plus action acknowledgement and dwell: Critical -> Pressure -> Soft -> Normal, at most one step per evaluation.
- Stale, malformed, unavailable, overflowed, or late evidence holds recovery. Warning events bypass unrelated event coalescing; same-trigger bursts coalesce.

## Bounds and overhead

- Positive cadence and six finite positive event intervals are independently rate-limited start-to-start. Sampling budget cannot exceed either interval. History is a fixed ring capped at 1,024 records; metrics use fixed enum cardinality and saturating counters.
- Ledger/physical exit floors must fit their finite configured ranges; ledger peak must cover committed bytes.
- Final macOS 256-sample system probe: total 0.000319625 seconds; maximum 0.000012042 seconds. macOS reports advisory unsupported rather than substituting host memory. iOS compiles one fresh `os_proc_available_memory()` call per accepted observation.

