--- a/LOGBOOK.md
+++ b/LOGBOOK.md
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 
 - IMPLEMENTATION: `MemoryWatermarkController` combines a new platform sample with timestamped ledger current/reserved/committed/peak bytes on one actor. iOS calls `os_proc_available_memory()` for every accepted observation; macOS reports the public API as unsupported instead of substituting host memory. Physical footprint and peak use `TASK_VM_INFO` on both platforms.
 - STATE: Inclusive Soft/Pressure/Critical entry takes the maximum of ledger headroom, configured-baseline physical headroom, advisory bytes, and memory warning. Recovery is strict-above the configured exit floor, requires fresh available evidence plus action acknowledgement and dwell, and moves at most one state per evaluation. Per-trigger event limiting prevents ordinary events from suppressing a simultaneous warning.
+- REVIEW REWORK: A reviewer negative test proved that a fresh warning could previously lower Pressure to Soft when the byte signals permitted recovery. `nextState` now clamps one-step recovery to the strongest entry signal in the same observation; a warning permits Critical to recover only to Pressure and cannot recover below Pressure. The committed regression test covers both boundaries.
 - BOUNDS/PRIVACY: Cadence, per-trigger event interval, evidence age, sampling-duration classification, history capacity (maximum 1,024), sequence, and fixed enum cardinality are explicit. Malformed, stale, unavailable, overflowed, or late evidence cannot recover state. Metrics and observations accept no destination, host, payload, credential, or free-form label.
 - REWORK: Self-review rejected a zero event interval, thresholds outside their finite ledger/physical ranges, and a ledger peak below committed bytes. The first tightened focused run then failed because cadence was measured finish-to-start and coalesced callers after one full-budget sample; production now measures start-to-start, so sampling work itself consumes the interval without allowing an unbounded zero interval.
 - VERIFICATION: Twelve deterministic Swift Testing cases cover real platform sampling, threshold equality/one-over, jumps, hysteresis, stale/unavailable evidence, warning bursts, action acknowledgement, configuration replacement, 64 concurrent observations, checked overflow, history, cardinality, and recovery. The final 256-sample macOS probe measured 0.000319625 seconds total and 0.000012042 seconds maximum. Generic iOS Simulator `ReluxTunnelCore` build succeeded; recursive Swift format passed; `make validate-core` passed 518 tests in 43 suites plus the post-test build, with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues.
